=head1 NAME

RepeatClassifier-nail - Classify Repeat Models ( nail prototype )

=head1 SYNOPSIS

  RepeatClassifier-nail [-options] -consensi <repeat model file>
                   [-stockholm <stockholm file>]

=head1 DESCRIPTION

The options are:

=over 4

=item -h(elp)

Detailed help

=item -threads #

Number of threads to use in the search.

=item -no_clash_rule

When protein hits to a consensus fall in clashing classes, the class
with evidence at least 10 orders of magnitude more significant wins.
This option disables that rule; clashing classes then merge to a
common root or become Unknown, as before.

=item -nail_dir <path>

Directory containing the nail binary.  Defaults to the NAIL_DIR
environment variable, then /usr/local/nail-v0.7.1.

=item -mmseqs <path>

Path to the MMseqs2 binary, which nail uses for seeding.  Defaults to
the MMSEQS_PRGM environment variable, then mmseqs on the PATH.

=item -nail_sensitivity #

MMseqs2 prefilter sensitivity, 1-10 ( default 10 ).  Lower values are
faster and less sensitive.

=item -evidence <prefix>

Write the evidence behind every classification to <prefix>.tsv ( one row
per family ) and <prefix>.json ( protein hits, DNA score buckets, the
clashes it settled, and the rule behind each call ).  Useful for
auditing a run or comparing two.

=back

